revision: a9c22b50428e0d2e42b8ca34a0fc8112373e4465
device: adb serial AYAUFIN76LEYR46X (2311DRK48G), dev client com.niks0501.caneguard 2.2.1 (installed 2026-11-15)
app runtime: installed dev client reused over Metro (`npm run start:dev-client -- --port 8081`, project script supplies
  certs/certificate.pem signing key path), stub API on :8210 via `npm run web:validate`, adb reverse 8081+8210.
rationale: `git diff --stat de6cb2..a9c22b5 -- package.json package-lock.json app.json app.config.js plugins
  metro.config.js babel.config.js eas.json` is empty, so the change carries no native delta and the runbook's
  "rebuild only on native change" reuse path applies. A local `./gradlew :app:assembleDebug` build is not possible in
  this environment: ANDROID_HOME (~/.local/share/android-platform-tools) holds platform-tools only,
  gradle/sdkmanager are absent and no android/ project exists (see r3-device-availability-and-scope.log).

## Web (first): guarded scan fails closed
npm run web:validate (CANEGUARD_WEB_VALIDATE_TODAY=2026-11-01) -> http://127.0.0.1:8199/login, farmer sign-in
/scan -> "Pumili ng isang larawan mula sa gallery" -> uploaded 1024x768 cane fixture
result: checklist shows "The sugarcane photo check is not available on this phone, so scans are paused. Update or
  reinstall the app, then try again."; choosing a picture leaves "Continue to analysis result" disabled -> scans paused.
  A 320x240 upload first shows the photo-quality rejection ("This photo may be hard to read" / low resolution),
  which keeps precedence over the unavailable-model message.
evidence: r3-web-03-guard-unavailable-fail-closed.png

## Phone: gallery sugarcane photo accepted -> V2 result (5 labels)
gallery 1024x768 cane fixture -> guard accepts -> "Photo checked. Choose a picture, then continue." -> Mosaic chosen
-> "Posibleng kondisyon: Smut" result screen.
Real field photograph: dev-assets/model-fixtures/v1-smut.jpg (3000x4000) -> guard accepts -> result Smut (0.9823).
Persisted rows (r3-caneguard-final.db, `scan_class_scores`): smut 0.9823, rssi 0.0142, rust 0.0018, healthy 0.0017,
  mosaic 0.0001 -> five-label V2 output.
evidence: r3-device-01-guard-accept-checklist.png, r3-device-02-guard-accept-v2-result.png,
  r3-device-05-real-photo-guard-accept.png

## Phone: gallery non-sugarcane photo rejected, no Continue, no saved scan
1024x1024 high-contrast non-sugarcane image (mean luminance 150, sd 82) -> guard rejects:
  "This does not look like sugarcane" + "CaneGuard could not see sugarcane in this photo, so it was not analysed..."
"Continue to analysis result" is absent (raw node: enabled=false, height 0); scan_records count stayed 0 after the
  rejection (r3-caneguard-after-reject.db).
evidence: r3-device-03-guard-rejects-not-sugarcane.png

## Phone: airplane mode repeat
cmd connectivity airplane-mode enable + `adb reverse --remove tcp:8210` (true API offline; Metro kept on 8081)
accept: cane fixture -> "Photo checked..." -> result "Posibleng kondisyon: Smut"
reject: non-sugarcane image -> "This does not look like sugarcane", Continue absent; scan_records still 1 (no new save)
restored: airplane-mode disable + reverse 8210 re-added.
evidence: r3-device-04-airplane-guard-reject.png

## Phone: EXIF-rotated portrait accepted
qa/guard-v1/cane-like-exif-rotated.jpg (Orientation=8, stored 240x320) upscaled to 768x1024 with the original APP1
  EXIF segment re-attached -> gallery -> guard accepts ("Photo checked. Choose a picture, then continue.") and the
  V2 result is reached; the Python oracle scores the same content 0.979 upright vs 0.259 when orientation is dropped,
  so the accept is only reachable with EXIF applied.
saved record: smut 0.9392, rssi 0.0604, healthy 0.0003, mosaic 0.0001, rust 0.0

